  "id": "consequent",
  "term": "consequent",
  "definition": "Consequent refers to a type of slope in which the rock layers and the slope are aligned, with parallel strike and the same dip direction. In gentle-dip consequent slopes, this arrangement can make sliding along bedding planes more likely because friction between layers is low.",
